KG42.register("rules-b1431f1c3334aaa6ecd04931",{"id":"31-coalition_formation::v141-c-R009","paper":"31-coalition_formation","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R009","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Market payment","process_stage":"settlement","market_meaning":"The local mid-market buying price p_b(t) determines the buyer's monetary cost as J_{n,b}(t) = p_b(t)E_{n,def}(t). Scope: P2P trading among state 1 prosumers within coalition 1. Condition: A state 1 prosumer buys deficient energy at time slot t. The prosumer must pay government tax and a subscription fee, captured by beta, for this transmission-line use. Scope: Grid transmission-line use under the proposed P2P charging and discharging price arrangement. Condition: A prosumer uses the transmission line provided by the grid for P2P trading.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function settlement.payment under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R009-E001","source":"pricing.local","target":"settlement.payment","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R009-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-M01-E24","v141-b-g01-E010"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"settlement","context_text":"Grid transmission-line use under the proposed P2P charging and discharging price arrangement. | P2P trading among state 1 prosumers within coalition 1.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-M01-E24","v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g02-E30"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x001","symbol":"J_{n,b}(t)","meaning":"Cost to prosumer n at state 1 at time slot t for buying deficient energy under the local mid-market buying price; dependent settlement/payment outcome in equation (4).","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued monetary cost (source does not state a numerical bound or sign restriction in this equation)","unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g02-E01"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R009-x002","symbol":"E_{n,def}(t)","meaning":"Energy deficiency of prosumer n at time slot t; the deficient energy bought at state 1 and multiplied by p_b(t) in equation (4).","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued energy quantity (source defines deficiency in equation (3); no explicit bound is stated in this rule)","unit":null,"indices":["n","t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E007","v141-b-g01-E010"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R009-t001","symbol":"p_b(t)","meaning":"Local mid-market buying price per unit of energy at time slot t, following the mid-market pricing scheme; price input to the buyer's payment in equation (4).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"currency per unit of energy (specific currency not stated in supplied text)","indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E010","v141-b-g02-E01","v141-b-M01-E24"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"The local mid-market buying price p_b(t) determines the buyer's monetary cost as J_{n,b}(t) = p_b(t)E_{n,def}(t). Scope: P2P trading among state 1 prosumers within coalition 1. Condition: A state 1 prosumer buys deficient energy at time slot t.","expression":"J_{n,b}(t) = p_b(t)\\,E_{n,def}(t)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R009-x001","v141-c-R009-x002"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R009-t001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-M01-E24","v141-b-g01-E010"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R009-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The prosumer must pay government tax and a subscription fee, captured by beta, for this transmission-line use. Scope: Grid transmission-line use under the proposed P2P charging and discharging price arrangement. Condition: A prosumer uses the transmission line provided by the grid for P2P trading.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["settlement.payment"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E30"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-M01-E24","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.3 Coalition formation algorithm","anchor_text":"W. Tushar, et al. trading, which is determined by a mid-market rate rule [39], a pro- ha sumer decid","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 1","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"unknown"},"source_text":"Prosumers that are in state 1 form coalition 1 (Fig. 1) and conduct P2P trading among themselves using the mechanism proposed in [39] via a mid-market pricing scheme. As for prosumers in state 2, each prosumer needs to decide either be a provider or a receiver of energy and thus be in the set $\\mathcal{K}$ or $\\mathcal{L}$ respectively. Once the decision is taken by prosumers, as shown in Fig. 2, each prosumer $n$ who was in state 1 in the previous time slot $t-1$ and would like to be in state 2 at $t$, splits itself from its previous coalition and merges with the players who decide to be in state 2 and thus becomes a part of a new coalition. A similar transition can also happen for state 2 players. Finally, P2P trading between the receivers and providers within coalition 2 is conducted using prices derived in (18) and (19)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E010","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1 Utility of prosumer at state 1","anchor_text":"battery energy across different entities. Hence, from the perspective of to P2P trading, each prosum","equation_id":"4","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"For prosumer at state 1 the contribution of a prosumer’s battery to the energy trading can be assumed to be 0 when considering the flow of battery energy across different entities. Hence, from the perspective of P2P trading, each prosumer n at state 1 can be considered as a prosumer with the grid-tie solar system without battery [43]. Therefore, prosumers of this type trade their solar energy either with one another prosumer or with the grid without charging or discharging their batteries. In this context, if the mid-market buying and selling prices per unit of energy are p_b(t) and p_s(t) respectively (following [39]), the utility and cost to a prosumer n can be defined as\nU_{n,s}(t) = p_s(t)E_{n,sur}(t), and J_{n,b}(t) = p_b(t)E_{n,def}(t) (4)\nrespectively for selling and buying their surplus and deficient energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p08-c1r1__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.4 Trading of energy","anchor_text":"W. Tushar, et al. coalition can be expressed by (2 L L m = 1 (bm , c ( t ) sm, c ( t )) ( pl + pc ( ","equation_id":"16-17","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Now, let us consider that the P2P charging price $p_c(t)$ and discharging price $p_d(t)$ per unit of energy are related to one another via [52] $p_c(t)=(1+\\beta)p_d(t)$ (17), where $\\beta>0$. The relationship in (17) is motivated by the fact that a prosumer needs to pay the government tax and a subscription fee, captured via $\\beta$, for using the transmission line provide by the grid for P2P purpose."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E007","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":"2. System model","anchor_text":"cordingly, d n,sur ( t ) = ( En ,pv (t ) + En,dis ( t )) ( En,hou ( t ) + En ,cha ( t )), (2) u- E a","equation_id":"2-3","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Accordingly, based on the generation, demand, and consumption of energy, each prosumer n may need to buy excess energy to meet its energy deficiency E_{n,def}(t) or has surplus energy E_{n,sur}(t) to sell. Accordingly,\nE_{n,sur}(t) = (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)) - (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)), (2)\nand\nE_{n,def}(t) = (E_{n,hou}(t) + E_{n,cha}(t)) - (E_{n,pv}(t) + E_{n,dis}(t)). (3)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E01","location":{"location_id":"src-e3722a409d-p04-c1r3__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1 Utility of prosumer at state 1","anchor_text":"battery energy across different entities. Hence, from the perspective of to P2P trading, each prosum","equation_id":"4","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this context, if the mid-market buying and selling prices per unit of energy are $p_b(t)$ and $p_s(t)$ respectively (following [39]), the utility and cost to a prosumer $n$ can be defined as $U_{n,s}(t)=p_s(t)E_{n,sur}(t)$, and $J_{n,b}(t)=p_b(t)E_{n,def}(t)$ (4), respectively for selling and buying their surplus and deficient energy."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"settlement.payment","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-E010","quote":"In this context, if the mid-market buying and selling prices per unit of energy are p_b(t) and p_s(t) respectively (following [39]), the utility and cost to a prosumer n can be defined as\nU_{n,s}(t) = p_s(t)E_{n,sur}(t), and J_{n,b}(t) = p_b(t)E_{n,def}(t) (4)\nrespectively for selling and buying their surplus and deficient energy."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-M01-E24","quote":"Prosumers that are in state 1 form coalition 1 (Fig. 1) and conduct P2P trading among themselves using the mechanism proposed in [39] via a mid-market pricing scheme."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-E30","quote":"a prosumer needs to pay the government tax and a subscription fee, captured via $\\beta$, for using the transmission line provide by the grid for P2P purpose."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"9e3d40aa582cf9f1b95e63945ce4dc34855307823cca5d55b58277a2abfd4bc2","applicability":"formalized","reason":"Constraint C001 is directly supported by the supplied equation (4): J_{n,b}(t)=p_b(t)E_{n,def}(t), with p_b(t) as the local mid-market buying price and E_{n,def}(t) as deficient energy. The frozen edge v141-c-R009-E001 links pricing.local to settlement.payment and is used for the formal binding. C002 remains not_formalized because the supplied text gives a beta-motivated price wedge p_c(t)=(1+beta)p_d(t) and beta>0, but the frozen C002 members contain only settlement.payment and no separate fee-amount expression is supplied; treating the price-wedge relation here would require the pricing.local membership and is already represented in the pricing rule. B evidence remains unreviewed in this experiment.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-C001","node_ids":["pricing.local","settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"Equation (4) is the payment relation in which p_b(t) from pricing.local determines the monetary cost at settlement.payment; edge v141-c-R009-E001 is the frozen local-price-to-payment link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x001","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"J_{n,b}(t) is the buyer cost defined by the settlement payment relation and is the target outcome of the frozen price-to-payment link."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-x002","node_ids":["settlement.payment"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"E_{n,def}(t) is the deficient energy quantity priced in the settlement payment formula; it enters the payment outcome along the frozen price-to-payment relation."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R009-t001","node_ids":["pricing.local"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R009-E001"],"rationale":"p_b(t) is the local mid-market buying price at pricing.local and is the source-side price input of the frozen pricing.local -> settlement.payment edge."}],"revision_requests":[]},"C2_delivery":{"raw_sha256":"bebf691975daca1cd0697d20cb6f0b838c3c7bfa7a9784235182581f89693a2b","delivery_payload_sha256":"8f71fc104ce120f6084bc7beb7d3a691272feb824d56be20b31464b1c5930da3","changes":[{"path":"theta.0.value.kind","before":"symbolic","after":"unspecified","reason":"Variant tag follows supplied value fields; no value, symbol or scientific statement is added, removed or rewritten."}],"scientific_fields_unchanged":true,"request_graph_sha256":"9e3d40aa582cf9f1b95e63945ce4dc34855307823cca5d55b58277a2abfd4bc2","scientific_correctness_verified":false}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
